Task1: Holmes Ditch A JD Request
WEST will prepare arequest for an approved jurisdictional determination (AJD).Based on our
initial assessment of the ditch and discussions with the City, it is likely that a non-jurisdictional
determination can be obtained for the ditch.Features are exempt from jurisdiction if theymeet
the following exclusion s:
(b)(3)ditches(including roadside ditches)excavated wholly in and draining only dry land
and that do not carry a relatively permanent flow of water;
(b)(8) swales and erosional features(e.g., gullies, small washes) characterized by low
volume, infrequent, or short duration flow.
WEST wil develop materials to support the A JD request including the wetland report, aerial
imagery showing excavation in uplands, and communicate with the City to document lack of
relatively permanent flow and draining only dryland.This information will be compiled intoasingle
Once submitted, WESTwill address questions and/or conduct a site visit with the USACE, if
required.We assume one meeting may be required to complete the AJD review process.
Assuminga non-jurisdictional determination isreceived, a Section 404permit would not be
required to perform maintenance activities.
